  "body": "## Two confirmed defects\n\n**1. Deferred-upgrade outcomes were unreadable on Windows.** The staged-update helper wrote its result receipt via `Set-Content -Encoding utf8` — under Windows PowerShell 5.1 (what `shutil.which(\"powershell\")` resolves first) that emits a **UTF-8 BOM** — while `pending_upgrade_result()` parsed with `read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")` + `json.loads`, refusing a leading U+FEFF. Every deferred upgrade therefore reported `None`; the outcome surface could never fire.\n\n**2. `Retry-After: 0` crashed failure classification.** The core parser accepts seconds >= 0 (a real upstream answer: *nothing to wait for*), but all four rate-limit mark sites fed values straight into `extend_reactive_block`, which raises <= 0 — turning a 429 carrying `retry-after: 0` into an exception out of error handling.\n\n## The fix\n\nReader `encoding=\"utf-8-sig\"`; helper emits BOM-less UTF-8 (`UTF8Encoding($false)` + `WriteAllText`) at both sites; new `_mark_rate_limited_when_positive` skips marks <= 0 at all four classification sites.\n\n## Honest deviations (§158)\n\nThe briefed raising cooldown validator was **not added**: blank values already coerce via existing machinery, and boot-refusal contradicts clamp-don't-refuse for hand-edited files — three named contract tests pin zero/negative/blank instead (`tests/config/test_limit_bounds.py`). The fourth mark site is unreachable via the public caller today (guarded anyway, documented). Observation parked for the structural wave: backoff delays ignore server Retry-After mid-loop.\n\n## Verification\n\nruff format/check, ty green; touched files **280 tests passed in 30.61s**; §66 mutations x3 caught by name (reader reverted -> BOM regression fails by name; clamp removed -> retry-after:0 fails; helper BOM restored -> writer test fails). The prior agent attempt died mid-flight leaving an uncommitted draft whose docstring claimed utf-8-sig while the code still said utf-8 — every hunk audited before reuse. PATCH slot **5.51.4**, sequential after main's current 5.51.3.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nPre-fix staged receipts parse via the sig-tolerant reader; new ones are BOM-less — both directions covered.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
